NEARS-1575 QA — regression (pre-existing DLS defect, newly surfaced by this call site)
Device emulator-5556, density 480dpi (px/3 = dp). Screen 1344x2992px = 448x997dp.

Live a11y measurement, Pharmacy home, "Open 24h" chip SELECTED (uiautomator, unclipped —
node lies wholly inside the chip band, no sticky-header intersection):

  'Open 24h'      y=1294-1426  (44dp)  x=352-666   clk=true  View     <- chip body, meets floor
  'Clear Filter'  y=1339-1381  (14dp)  x=588-630   clk=true  Button   <- remove glyph, BELOW floor

Source (packages/nears_dls/lib/elements/nfilterchip/n_filter_chip.dart), unmodified by this
branch (`git diff --stat e2e18cc1 -- packages/nears_dls` is empty):

    if (onRemove != null) ...[
      Semantics(
        button: true,
        label: removeSemanticLabel,
        child: GestureDetector(
          onTap: onRemove,
          behavior: HitTestBehavior.opaque,
          child: NIcon('close', px: 14, color: foreground),   // no padding / no min size
        ),
      ),
    ],

The GestureDetector wraps the 14px glyph directly, so the hit area IS 14dp — matching the
measured node exactly. NOT AC-breaking: the chip's own 44dp body performs the same action
(onTap toggles the selected chip back to unfiltered, verified live), so the small glyph is a
redundant affordance, not the only way to clear.
